title start
kind: default
tags: notation contracts
Plan: aiu notation contracts
title end

section start
title start
Section 1: decided so far
title end

paragraph start
Command: aiu notation contracts, and every contract action is a subcommand of it.
paragraph end

paragraph start
A contract is a block written contract start and contract end. It is attached to the block kind it is for, the same way a todo is attached: a contract for a paragraph sits on the paragraph, a contract for a title sits on the title.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Storage: a .notation/ folder, created automatically in the directory where the command runs, with one subfolder per block type and one file per contract. The section condition is written inside the contract itself.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Inheritance: a .notation/ applies to its directory and every subdirectory, until a subdirectory has its own .notation/.
paragraph end

paragraph start
When a block of a type that has contracts is made in the text editor, the editor asks the notation system, and the notation system writes the contracts inside the file under that block. The contract text cannot be edited in the file.
paragraph end

paragraph start
The notation system gets a contracts directory holding the code, with a types subfolder holding the default contracts. Every block category gets at least one default contract, so the feature can be seen working.
paragraph end

paragraph start
No max-words, min-words, max-lines or other counting rules. A contract is free text, as long as it needs to be, because some contracts need a lot of explaining.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Every contract is a todo until it is populated. The todo mark moves to the upper right of the box for every todo, and titles stay on the left like everything else.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Errors and warnings must show inside the text editor, and an LSP style server is wanted so other editors can use them too.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Contracts are created in the text editor. No creation TUI. A TUI comes later, only to select and deselect which contracts are used, after the whole ecosystem works.
paragraph end

paragraph start
The hard coded the-contracts lists in filetypes/types are deleted once their questions exist as contract files.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Section 2: answered questions, see section 13
title end

paragraph start
All nine questions of this section are answered in section 13 on 2026-11-12: every current question becomes a contract file that keeps its id, the file is named by its id, the file type condition sits inside the contract, the editor attaches contracts when it makes a block and every save re-syncs them, read only is enforced by the editor and by check, the todo mark applies to every todo, editor integration comes first and the LSP server later, a subdirectory without a folder for a type falls back to the parent, and the required section lists move into .notation/ as contracts.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Section 3: the database comes first
title end

paragraph start
Status: resumed 2026-11-12. The database engine core and the indexers are done (section 12), so the contracts work continues, see section 13.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Goal: one database for absolutely everything, like Vulpea v2 in Emacs but better. It indexes files, blocks, links, tags, todos, contracts and answers, and every file and link can be queried directly from it.
paragraph end

paragraph start
SQLite is not used. A much better database system is wanted, and it is not chosen yet.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Needs: links and backlinks between files and blocks, fast search, direct queries on any file or block, files stay plain text as the source of truth, the index rebuilds from the files at any time.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Section 4: database decisions
title end

paragraph start
Engine: our own, written in Rust, no outside database and no SQLite.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Data model: not decided yet. It must be built on the box system that already exists, not a plain graph of simple nodes. The tree view and the mind map view are wanted, so the model has to serve both.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Source of truth: the files. This is a hard rule. The database can always be rebuilt from the files and holds nothing that exists nowhere else.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Indexed first: files, blocks, links, tags and todos. More kinds come later. Each kind gets its own source file in the code, so the code for each kind stays separate.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Updates: when the editor saves and when aiu notation runs. A file watcher comes later, not now.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Scope: a database file in every directory, not one for the whole ecosystem.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Query: commands and a TUI. The notation CLI and the editor read the same database and must work together at all times.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Still open: the data model, the file format of the database, how a directory database relates to its subdirectories, and what the first query commands are.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Engine decision: written from zero in Rust inside notation, with no outside engine, so every feature stays under our control. Cozo, Datascript and the others were looked at and rejected.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Section 5: names, links and reuse
title end

paragraph start
Everything is linkable and reusable. A whole file, a chapter, a section, a paragraph or any other block can be taken from one file and shown inside another.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Identity: every box kind gets its own declaration holding a unique, readable name. The name is built from several parts so that no two are the same. It is written in the file, so it survives edits above it. The name is the id and the link target at once.
paragraph end

paragraph start
No random ids and no Emacs style identifiers. A link uses the real name of what it points to.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Links are blocks: link start and link end, the same way as every other block. A link names its target box and may ask for it to be shown in place.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Every existing block kind must be edited to accept the name declaration.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Typing support: an LSP style server suggests existing names while typing a link, in the editor and in other editors.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Admin files stay in the .notation/ directory: the database index.db, the contracts and anything else the notation system owns.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Section 6: decisions on names and shown boxes
title end

paragraph start
This section answers the open paragraph of section 5.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Name parts: the kind plus the first words of the title or text, with a short counter added only when two names collide. Example: paragraph-install-guide, section-goal. Chosen for being modular, so the builder is one small replaceable function.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Scope: a name is unique across the whole ecosystem. A contract checks it. A link needs no path, only the name.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Rename: renaming a name rewrites every link and every shown copy in every file, through the database. The check reports any link left pointing at a missing name.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Shown boxes are never read only. A box shown inside another file can be edited right there. On save the notation system updates the original file and every other file that shows the same box. If paragraph 1 is shown in ten files, all ten and the original receive the saved text.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Who writes names: the editor writes the name when a block is made. The notation system fills in old blocks that have none.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Source of truth stays the files. The database finds which files show a box, and the files hold all the text.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Section 8: decisions on saving, cycles and deletion
title end

paragraph start
Shown text is stored inside the file between link start and link end, so a file is complete without the database. It is synced on save.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Autosave: in write mode, if nothing is typed for 5 seconds, a notification appears, write mode ends and the file is saved. Everything is always saved.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Cycles: a shown box may contain a link and nest, but a cycle (A shows B shows A) is refused with an error.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Uniqueness applies to originals only. A copy is recognised by sitting inside a link block.
paragraph end

paragraph start
A save that touches many files also updates every open buffer that holds a changed box.
paragraph end

paragraph start
After a multi file save the list of changed files is printed, and one undo reverts all of them.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Deleting: nothing is deleted unless it is tracked by git, so the deletion can be undone, unless the owner approves explicitly. This holds for a file, a section, a paragraph or any block.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Deleting something that is shown in other files opens a large popup with red borders and red text, listing the files and asking yes or no. The shown copies stay as normal blocks if the answer is yes.
paragraph end

paragraph start
The names registry lives in the database at the ecosystem root, and each directory database reports up to it.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Section 10: answers to section 9
title end

paragraph start
Name keyword: name: on its own line under the start line of every block kind, including a whole file on its title block. Example: name: paragraph-install-guide. A link block holds name: and target:. Confirmed.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Delete and its git check: they belong to our own file manager, which is built later. The file manager does the tracked check and shows the red popup when a box is shown elsewhere.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Untracked files: the approval word is decided together with the file manager design. The delete is refused until then.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Idle timer: a setting, default 5 seconds, counting keystrokes only. The timer starts when typing stops.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Autosave: every autosave also syncs the shown copies in other files.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Order of work: agreed on 2026-11-06: engine core, indexers one kind at a time, names, links and sync, red delete popup, autosave.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Section 11: block types in .notation
title end

paragraph start
Block types are detected from a .notation/blocktypes/ folder, the same way contracts are: one file per block type, found at the nearest directory base and inherited by every subdirectory.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Making a new block type, changing one or deleting one is adding, editing or deleting one file in that folder. No code is edited.
paragraph end

paragraph start
The folder notation/blocktypes/ holds the default types and seeds every new .notation/. The parser and the register take their block names at run time from the folder they find; the build time list is gone.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Still open: a subdirectory with its own .notation/ but no file for some type, whether it falls back to the parent, the same open question as for contracts; and how each type says how it is drawn.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Section 12: progress 2026-11-06
title end

paragraph start
Done: the database engine core (record.rs, store.rs, file-format.rs), the indexers for files, blocks, links, names, tags, todos, and the folder command notation index <folder> that walks a directory, indexes every .aiu and saves .notation/index.db.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Done: block types load at run time from the nearest .notation/blocktypes folder, the counting rules are removed, and a duplicate name is printed by the folder command.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Open, in order: name filler for old blocks that have none, duplicate name as a check error, link as a registered block type, block types loaded per file in the folder command, then links and sync, the red delete popup in our own file manager, and idle autosave after 5 seconds.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Section 13: contract work order, decided 2026-11-12
title end

paragraph start
Storage: one contract file per question, inside .notation/TYPE/ of the nearest directory base, named by its id. There is no single questions page. Every current question becomes a contract file and keeps its id, so no answer is orphaned.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Creation: contracts are made and edited in the text editor, as files. There is no creation command and no TUI.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Condition and text: the file type condition sits inside the contract next to the section condition. A contract is free text with no counting rules.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Attaching: the editor attaches the contracts when it makes a block. aiu notation and every save sync them again, so a changed contract file updates every attached copy. Read only: the editor refuses edits inside a contract block, and check reports an attached contract that differs from its file.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Todo mark: the right side mark applies to every todo. A contract counts as populated when its block has an answer.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Inheritance: a .notation/ applies to its directory and every subdirectory. A subdirectory with its own .notation/ but no folder for some type falls back to the parent. Block types follow the same rule.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Lists: the required section lists move into .notation/ as contracts. The hard coded the-contracts lists in filetypes/types are deleted after the contract files exist. LSP: editor integration first, the server later. The contract work is no longer paused, the database core and the indexers are done.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Order of work: step 1, block type holes: fill name on old blocks, duplicate name as a check error, register link as a block type and let the indexer read link blocks, load block types per file, move how each type is drawn into its blocktypes file. Step 2, contracts: seed the contract files with ids kept, the loader, the missing contract error, delete the hard coded lists, fix filetypes/types/README.md. Step 3: links and sync, the red delete popup in our own file manager, idle autosave, the ecosystem server.
paragraph end

section end
